outcome:
Every place that can create or start a mailbox wake asks one predicate over the session authority: never-woken recovery, the boot unread pass, explicit requeue, coalescing in dispatch_turn (both branches), queue-head revalidation and activation. Unread data is a candidate, never permission to dispatch.
The predicate distinguishes four cases:
- known unsent: the obligation is kept even when the mail was acknowledged;
- confirmed delivered with eligible unread mail: may open the separately identified recovery obligation, under existing policy;
- confirmed delivered with acknowledged mail: creates no new wake;
- unknown with unread mail: stays unknown.
An unresolved attempt blocks automatic recovery of its overlapping scope. A later, higher-sequence message must not coalesce over it and thereby replay the unresolved scope; the successor waits behind the unresolved barrier until reconciliation. A cancelled obligation is never reopened by an unread scan. max(sequence) is never taken as proof that every underlying scope is eligible.

Provenance: Architect2's decision f639826d on w-3bd74078208d; item 4 of the decomposition in TermAl mailbox 03723eab #42, accepted in #43.
Review findings it carries: round-3 High (Codex 39fa80aa): the boot unread pass does not exclude a boundary held as unresolved, so an unknown handoff is replayed and its attempt witness overwritten.
Criteria to be proposed by the holder and concurred by the coordinator.
